i am thinking of a particular class C of function

a function f is in C if:

x!=0 => (p(f(x)) = p(x) OR f(x) = 0), where p is the canonical projectivization projection, i.e. f(x) lies always on the same unoriented line thru the origin as x

f is R^n to R^n & p is the canonical projection onto RP^n-1

f is continuous & smooth except at its singularity at the origin



i mean really these are just continuous angle-preserving functions on the unoriented blowup






